# Cline project rules — Cape Jones

These rules apply to every Cline session in this repo (extension, CLI, or
headless). The full law book lives in AGENTS.md at the repo root. Read it
before every task; it outranks these notes.

## The non-negotiables, verbatim from the owner

1. Branch → PR → merge. NEVER commit to main directly.
2. VERIFY-BEFORE-CLAIMING: a worker's "done" is a claim. Check the source of
   truth yourself (file exists? PR state MERGED? upload listed at destination?).
   Tag confidence: verified / single-source / unverified / contradicted.
3. CHECK-RESEARCH-WIRE-DO, in that order. Never do-first-research-after.
4. ANTI-SYCOPHANCY: never agree with an unverified premise ("it's lost, right?").
   Check your own lane first.
5. PUSH-AFTER-EVERY-TURN. No open PRs sitting, no hoarded work.
6. NO-HAND-TOOLING-EDITS: rebuild from clean state; never manual patch edits.
7. Conflicts keep BOTH sides. Never delete another agent's work.
8. CHECK-BEFORE-STARTING: git log, open PRs, checkpoints — no duplicate lanes.

Before starting work, run: git log --oneline -5 && gh pr list --state open

## Cline-specific layer (cape-jones)

### Git discipline

- Work happens on a worktree branch off `origin/main`. Never push to another
  lane's branch (e.g. anything under `build/`, `feature/`, `setup/` you
  didn't create). Verify the merge landed on main after the PR merges.
- Do NOT touch `.vscode/` (owned by the IDE-config lane).

### Renders

- Never claim a render is good without looking at actual frames with your
  own eyes. Diff frames, check for black frames, verify duration with
  `ffprobe`.

### Locked colorway — never invent colors

The living-room colorway is LOCKED. Use only these:

| Name | Hex |
|---|---|
| Coral pink | `#F15E57` |
| Blue | `#5B84DD` |
| Warm oak | `#E59964` |
| Violet LED | `#731AE5` |
| Warm yellow | `#FFE996` |
| Brick | `#9B4C49` |
| Pale blue-grey | `#BDD2D6` |

Character color canon lives in `docs/lighting/COLOR-GRADES.md` (suit stays
`#FFFFFF`, cowl `#3E1473`, skin `#E5B28C`, cape `#000000`). Do not introduce
new palette colors without the owner's explicit approval.

### Blender discipline

- `.blend` files are BINARY. Never edit them directly, never hand-tweak in
  the GUI and re-save as "the fix". Scenes are driven by Blender Python
  scripts (e.g. `tools/layout-rules/apply_layout_blend.py`); change the
  script, re-run it, re-render.
- Headless Blender on this VM requires BOTH, every time:
  `xvfb-run -a env -u PYTHONPATH <blender> -b ...`
  (`xvfb-run` for the EGL/libEGL.so.1 crash, `env -u PYTHONPATH` so the
  system numpy doesn't leak into Blender's bundled Python.)
- Repo Blender pin is 4.5.12 LTS (see `.devcontainer/`). The one legacy
  install at `~/workspace/tools/blender/` is 4.0.2 — do not mix them up.
- Quaternion trap: Blender pose bones default to QUATERNION rotation —
  euler keyframes are silently ignored. Set `rotation_mode='XYZ'` explicitly.

### Keys and privacy

- API keys live in env vars or the tool's own credential store. NEVER in
  files, logs, chat, diffs, or PRs.
- The stored `custom.legacy-gemini` connector credential is surrogate-only
  (one-turn image edits). It is NOT retrievable as a raw API key — do not
  try to extract or reuse it as one.

### Scope

- YES: Python scripts, JSON configs, docs, shell glue, validators, tests.
- NO: `.blend`/`.fbx`/`.glb` binaries (script-driven only), `production/assets/`
  (ARCHIVE LAW — production materials keep their own home, never modified),
  `node_modules/`, session junk.
- When a plan is ambiguous, ask or leave it standing. Do exactly the asked
  job — surgical scope, no scope creep, no cheap shortcuts.
